{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1259074-homebrew-abjuriation-opinion-needed","id":1259074,"title":"Homebrew Abjuriation opinion needed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-05T07:20:35-07:00","id":1259074,"title":"Homebrew Abjuriation opinion needed","content":"In our homebrew Hunter, we mix True Faith from oWoD with 2nd edition abjuration, the Prayer Merit (long night), and Benediction Endowment. One question that came up was the dice pool to abjure non-ephemeral entities. In the oWoD the creatures would often use their Willpower pool as a defense. I suggested Presence + Composure + Potency to reflect what spirits use (Power + Resistance) because it parallels a strength and a resistance trait. What would you use for a defending monster? For our game, the basic abjure pool for a hunter is Resolve + Composure until the Hunter buys a benediction to give them a specialty (adding their Prayer dots) so the max a hunter's pool could be is about 20ish (given abjure bonuses).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12209-adonus","name":"adonus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T15:42:09-07:00","id":1259133,"title":"","content":"Resolve+Composure+Potency would make sense, as it is the most direct port of Will+powerstat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0